        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of iterating through all combinations of multiples of \\( A \\), which is computationally expensive, we can use modular arithmetic properties to determine if there exists a non-negative integer \\( k \\) such that \\( kA \\equiv C \\pmod{B} \\). This can be done using the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \\( A \\) and \\( B \\), and then checking if \\( C \\) is a valid residue modulo the GCD. If the GCD divides \\( C \\), then it is possible to achieve the desired sum.",
